{
  "$comment": "The launch taxonomy: game events, two levels at most, slash-separated, stable ids. A category id is either a top-level group (\"movement\") or \"group/leaf\" (\"movement/jump\"). A compound distinction the spec writes as \"hit/{light,heavy}\" or \"footstep/{grass,...}\" is not a third category level: it is a tag on individual sounds filed under the two-level leaf category (\"combat/hit\" tagged \"heavy\"; \"movement/footstep\" tagged \"grass\"). The API's event resolver (POST /api/v1/resolve, GET /api/v1/sounds?q=) accepts the short forms the spec itself uses in examples - a bare leaf name (\"jump\"), a fully qualified id (\"ui/confirm\"), or \"leaf/tag\" (\"hit/heavy\", \"footstep/grass\") - and maps all three to a category plus an optional tag filter. See docs/GAMESOUNDS.md.",
